ars.githubusercontent.com/u/243248197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/odinlabs-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odinlabs-ai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/runs/30586345158/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/runs/30586345158/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/check-suites/82939358783","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/runs/30586345158/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/runs/30586345158/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/runs/30586345158/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/actions/workflows/324061377","head_commit":{"id":"cd7779e6a855850548f90b77f8764c975cef54ae","tree_id":"a95a4c712e1b9e2a37847e37e7f78b30d0618a46","message":"test(tui): pty-driven interactive proof of the attach-planner dashboard — quality-matrix baseline\n\nThe bce behavioral teeth prove the SEAMS in isolation; they do not prove the\nINTERACTIVE flow. This harness closes that gap: it launches the REAL\n`odin-agent dashboard` against a REAL pseudo-terminal (node-pty, not a pipe),\ndrives keys, and asserts the LIVE rendered transitions — the honest proof that\nthe create-many / hop-in / steer / detach / inspect flow actually works.\n\nFiles:\n  - src/blueprint/pty-dashboard-driver.ts — reusable pty driver (spawn in a real\n    pty, waitFor(regex), press(keys), ANSI-stripped snapshot, clean teardown).\n  - src/blueprint/seed-dashboard-fleet.ts — deterministic filesystem fleet seeding\n    (writes the real registry records into a fresh temp cwd per run — hermetic).\n  - src/__tests__/attach-interactive-proof.test.ts — 6 scenarios; 4 always-on:\n      (a) BOOT+LIST  — dashboard renders on a real pty + lists the seeded fleet\n      (b1) HOP-IN    — enter fires the attach flow (legible seeded refusal)\n      (c) STEER      — i-inject dispatches with a real \"Dispatched: inject → …\" confirmation\n      (e) INSPECT    — enter on a done row renders the read-only log (content-unique marker)\n    + 2 opt-in @requires-launch (b2 live-attach, d Ctrl-A-d detach) gated behind a\n    flag — they spawn a real cycle (env-sensitive), pass when enabled.\n  - package.json — \"proof:interactive\": \"tsup && vitest run …\".\n\nANTI-CHEAT (adversarially verified — it can go RED on a REAL regression):\n  - silent-swallow the i-inject frame → STEER (c) times out RED; revert → green.\n  - drop one fleet row (shown.slice(1)) → BOOT/HOP-IN/STEER RED (\"SESSIONS · 3 active\"); revert → green.\n  - break the live attach markers → opt-in b2/d time out RED; restore → green.\nEach assertion is pinned to a string only the real render path produces.\n\nHermetic + re-runnable: fresh mkdtemp cwd per scenario, no network/LLM, daemon\nforced off, stable across repeated runs (verified x3). Run: `npm run proof:interactive`.\n\nHONESTY BOUNDARY (in the design doc): proves the key→transition→render flow on a\nreal pty; does NOT assert a real LLM turn (b2/d assert attach chrome, not model\noutput) nor the cross-process daemon socket (covered by daemon-live-attach.integration.test.ts).\n\ntsc 0 errors. vitest: 4 passed | 2 skipped, ~3s (ran locally, with my own eyes).\n\n(cherry picked from commit 8888140f74bb68c7f7379a524442685b3872a87a)","timestamp":"2026-07-30T22:12:00Z","author":{"name":"Mitchell Tieleman","email":"mitchell@odin-labs.ai"},"committer":{"name":"Mitchell Tieleman","email":"mitchell@odin-labs.ai"}},"repository":{"id":1142700498,"node_id":"R_kgDORBw50g","name":"odin-suite","full_name":"odin-labs-ai/odin-suite","private":true,"owner":{"login":"odin-labs-ai","id":256870016,"node_id":"O_kgDOD0-GgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256870016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/odin-labs-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odin-labs-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite","description":"Odin Suite deployment orchestration and infrastructure","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/odin-labs-ai/odin-suite/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/